## Props

| Prop | Type | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `state` | `CropperState` \| `null` | `null` |
| `image` | `CropperImage` \| `null` | `null` |
| `transitions` | `CropperTransitions` \| `null` | `null` |
| `loading` | `boolean` | `false` |
| `loaded` | `boolean` | `true` |
| `class` | `ClassValue` | `undefined` |
| `wrapper` | `Snippet<[CropperPreviewWrapperSnippetProps]>` | `CropperPreviewWrapper` |
| `boundary` | `Snippet<[CropperPreviewBoundarySnippetProps]>` | `StretchableBoundary` |
| `background` | `Snippet<[CropperPreviewBackgroundSnippetProps]>` | `CropperPreviewBackground` |
| `crossOrigin` | `CrossOrigin` | `true` |
| `style` | `string` | `undefined` |
| `cropper` | `CropperPreviewSource` \| `null` | `undefined` |


## Source and exports

`CropperPreviewSource` supplies `getState(): CropperState | null`, `getImage(): CropperImage | null`, `getTransitions(): CropperTransitions | null`, `isLoading(): boolean` and `isLoaded(): boolean`.

Source precedence is `cropper`, then the adapter installed with `update`, then the snapshot props. A source must be non-null to win. Reactive getters update the preview automatically.

| Export on `CropperPreviewInstance` | Behavior |
| --- | --- |
| `refresh(): void` | Re-read the source and stretch the boundary, including nonreactive adapters. |
| `update(cropper?: CropperPreviewSource` \| `null): void` | Store or clear the adapter and refresh. |

## Snippets and context

[Preview snippets](/docs/reference/snippets#preview-snippets) receive `preview` and, for the background, the fitted `size`. The default boundary uses `stretchPreviewBoundary`. Async results are ignored when superseded or destroyed. No cropper context is provided or required. There is no export method on a preview.

## Selectors

`.advanced-cropper-preview`, `__boundary`, `__content`, `__image` and `__image--visible` identify the preview. The wrapper additionally emits `.cropper-preview-wrapper` and `__fade`. See [styling](/docs/reference/styling).
